<speak>drugs mimic a hormone governing the brain's reward pathways, the same circuits that drive both appetite and craving for addictive substances. Randomised controlled trials are still needed, and pharmaceutical companies already struggle to meet global demand for obesity treatment alone.

In technology.
A single trader made two hundred thousand dollars correctly predicting the date of Iran's attack — by betting on a prediction market that lists real-money wagers on which cities will be bombed and which leaders will be killed. United States Senators Jeff Merkley and Amy Klobuchar proposed ten thousand dollar fines for government officials who trade on war markets, arguing the prices function as military intelligence readable by any adversary. Platforms like Polymarket and Kalshi remain open and unregulated for the general public.

OpenAI owes one hundred billion dollars and has no credible path to profit: training costs rise with every new model, and nine hundred million of its users pay nothing. The company needs fifteen times its current revenue by 2030 to cover its obligations, a threshold Nvidia chief Jensen Huang described as the baseline before a possible public listing. Whether a company that gave away artificial intelligence at scale can now charge for it remains the defining question of the industry.

That's your briefing from zuhd news.

We return this evening.

إن شاء الله.</speak>